From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the missing BSD-3-Clause LICENSE file

crates/icu_messageformat_python/Cargo.toml (and every other crate under
crates/icu_messageformat*) declares `license = "BSD-3-Clause"`, matching
the licence PyPI shows for every released icu_messageformat wheel, but
no LICENSE file for that licence exists anywhere in the git tree: not
in python/icu_messageformat, not in crates/icu_messageformat_python, not
at the repository root (the only LICENSE.md in the tree,
packages/intl/LICENSE.md, is the MIT text for the unrelated JS `intl`
package). The published wheels ship no licence text at all, for any
platform, confirmed against the real icu_messageformat-0.1.1
cp312-abi3-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl on PyPI (METADATA/WHEEL/RECORD
only, no .dist-info/licenses/).

Add the standard BSD 3-Clause text, with the same "FormatJS" copyright
holder packages/intl/LICENSE.md uses for the monorepo's other
first-party packages, so pyproject.toml's `license-files` has a real
file to pick up.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every icu_messageformat wheel on PyPI regardless of architecture, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 python/icu_messageformat/LICENSE | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 python/icu_messageformat/LICENSE

diff --git a/python/icu_messageformat/LICENSE b/python/icu_messageformat/LICENSE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a68ff76
--- /dev/null
+++ b/python/icu_messageformat/LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+BSD 3-Clause License
+
